    <string name="tour_step_count">%1$d of %2$d</string>
    <string name="tour_welcome_title">Welcome to %1$s</string>
    <string name="tour_welcome_body">This quick tour goes through each section of the companion and what it controls. Press A for the next step, B to go back, and Y to skip.</string>
    <string name="tour_rail_title">Sections</string>
    <string name="tour_rail_body">Settings are grouped into sections here. Moving through the list switches the pane on the right, and D-pad Right jumps into that section\'s settings.</string>
    <string name="tour_general_body">Core behavior: taking over the AYN button, status bar extras, backups, updates and the replay buffer.</string>
    <string name="tour_replace_stock_body">Turn this on so the AYN button opens Command Panel\'s overlay instead of the built-in dual-screen assistant. Turning it off gives the button back.</string>
    <string name="tour_overlay_extras_title">Overlay extras</string>
    <string name="tour_overlay_extras_body">Fine-tune the overlay: show a battery time estimate, hide the network speed readout, and choose which apps Clear All Tasks leaves running.</string>
    <string name="tour_backup_body">Save every companion setting to a JSON file, or restore your most recent backup after a reinstall.</string>
    <string name="tour_updates_body">See which version you\'re on, check for a new release and reopen the patch notes. Command Panel downloads and installs updates itself.</string>
    <string name="tour_replay_body">Keep the last few seconds in memory, then save a clip after something happens. Capture the top screen, the bottom one, or both stacked into one video, and pick how far back it reaches and the clip quality.</string>
    <string name="tour_save_clip_body">Save clips from a shortcut in another app, like Back Button Hero. This shows whether TCP SC is installed, and installs the one that matches your version of Command Panel.</string>
    <string name="tour_preview_body">Open the overlay on the bottom screen to try your changes for real.</string>
    <string name="tour_nav_bar_body">Arrange the buttons along the bottom of the overlay and set up a Quick Launch shortcut.</string>
    <string name="tour_button_order_body">Put the nav bar buttons in the order you want. With a controller, press A to pick one up, move it with the D-pad, and press A again to drop it.</string>
    <string name="tour_quick_launch_body">Add a Launch button that opens an app of your choice on the screen you pick. It can show that app\'s icon and name, too.</string>
    <string name="tour_tiles_body">Choose which tiles the overlay shows and the order they appear in.</string>
    <string name="tour_tile_labels_body">Show icons only for a cleaner grid. The icons grow to fill the space.</string>
    <string name="tour_tile_order_title">Tile order</string>
    <string name="tour_tile_order_body">Your enabled tiles in overlay order. Drag them, or use A and the D-pad, to rearrange them.</string>
    <string name="tour_tile_picker_title">Available tiles</string>
    <string name="tour_tile_picker_body">Every tile Command Panel offers, grouped into the stock AYN tiles, Android system tiles and extra tools. Flip a switch to add or remove a tile.</string>
    <string name="tour_appearance_body">The overlay\'s theme mode, and how its look and accent carry over to this screen.</string>
    <string name="tour_overlay_theme_body">Light, dark, or follow the system theme for the bottom-screen overlay.</string>
    <string name="tour_follow_look_body">Restyle this companion screen with the overlay\'s look, theme and accent, so both screens match.</string>
    <string name="tour_rgb_accent_body">Use the Thor\'s Ambient LED color as the overlay\'s accent, so the UI matches your joystick lights.</string>
    <string name="tour_themes_body">Pick a look for the overlay, mix your own in Theme Studio, and share or download looks.</string>
    <string name="tour_active_look_body">The look the overlay uses right now, previewed live. Customize opens it in Theme Studio.</string>
    <string name="tour_mix_body">Start a new look in Theme Studio by combining cards, tiles, gauges, sliders, nav and fonts from any look.</string>
    <string name="tour_my_looks_body">Looks you\'ve saved. Export them as a pack to share, or import a pack someone sent you.</string>
    <string name="tour_packs_body">Packs you put in the TCP Themes folder show up here, along with the fonts they use.</string>
    <string name="tour_repos_body">Follow a GitHub theme repo or a link to a pack. Its looks are added and stay up to date as the author changes them.</string>
    <string name="tour_default_repo_title">TCP Themes</string>
    <string name="tour_default_repo_body">Command Panel follows the TCP Themes repo from the start, so new looks show up on their own as they\'re added. Find them under Themes → Packs, or remove the repo here if you\'d rather not.</string>
    <string name="tour_builtin_body">All the looks that ship with Command Panel. Pick one to apply it to the overlay right away.</string>
    <string name="tour_diagnostics_body">Check that the privileged access Command Panel relies on is working.</string>
    <string name="tour_privileged_body">Checks hidden-API access, the root shell and the root helper. If a feature isn\'t working, start here.</string>
    <string name="tour_finish_title">You\'re all set</string>
    <string name="tour_finish_body">That\'s the tour. Take it again any time from General → Updates.</string>
